{"nodes": [{"id": "agents", "label": "AGENTS.md (BuonApp agent guide)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agents_offline_first_invariant", "label": "Offline-First Operation Invariant", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Core POS operation (orders, billing, tables and service days, kitchen tickets, printing) must work without internet. The cloud bridge and usage telemetry were removed with the settings that armed them (migration v80). Only owner-configured features (Google Drive backup; WhatsApp kept in code but switched off by WHATSAPP_AVAILABLE) and the update check against the fork's own GitHub releases may reach the network, and all must fail gracefully offline. No outbound channel to a vendor may be reintroduced."}, {"id": "agents_data_safety_invariant", "label": "Data Safety Invariant", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Existing customer data must survive upgrades: never reset, truncate or drop user databases as a shortcut for migration design."}, {"id": "agents_no_taxation_engine", "label": "No Taxation Engine (Architecture Boundary)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The fork computes no taxes: prices are what the guest pays, the bill is a preconto, and the fiscal receipt comes from the till beside it. No taxation engine, country tax packs or per-item tax fields."}, {"id": "agents_ui_language_regional_decoupling", "label": "UI Language Decoupled from Tenant Regional Settings", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Architecture boundary: UI language and tenant regional settings are separate, decoupled domains."}, {"id": "agents_one_order_one_bill", "label": "One Order, One Bill Invariant", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Splitting a check between guests was removed in 5.0.0 (migration v91), columns and all: an order has one bill and who pays what is settled at the till. Paying one bill with several payment methods is a different feature and stays."}, {"id": "agents_no_joined_tables", "label": "No Joined Tables (removed in migration v97)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "REMOVED FEATURE. Joining tables for one party went the same way as split checks: migration v97 removed it, column (tables.merged_into) and all, together with the merge/split API routes. A large party is seated by changing the map in edit mode (a bigger table, more seats), so a table that defers to another must not be brought back. Part of invariant 4 (One order, one bill)."}, {"id": "agents_business_timestamps", "label": "Business Timestamps Invariant", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Persisted timestamps follow canonical storage conventions; the configured store timezone applies to business-local presentation, day/shift boundaries and reporting intervals."}, {"id": "agents_backend_authority", "label": "Backend Authority Invariant", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Security-critical and payment calculations remain backend-authoritative."}, {"id": "agents_reuse_before_adding", "label": "Reuse Before Adding Invariant", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Reuse existing helpers, utilities and dependencies before introducing new packages."}, {"id": "agents_scope_discipline", "label": "Scope Discipline", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Implement only the approved task; no opportunistic refactors across unrelated files; adjacent issues go in the report."}, {"id": "agents_services_routes_boundary", "label": "Services/Routes Boundary for Fork Domains", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The fork-added domains (service days, rooms and the floor map, reservations, saved layouts, kitchen-ticket rounds, service runs, cover charge, fixed menus) keep their logic in main/services/ and use main/routes/ only for authorization and HTTP translation, without an import cycle between the two."}, {"id": "agents_source_of_truth", "label": "Source of Truth Hierarchy (CURRENT / ACTIVE DESIGN / HISTORICAL)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Current code and tests define runtime behavior; the approved task defines intended change; AGENTS.md and CURRENT docs define invariants; ACTIVE DESIGN / FORWARD-LOOKING docs may be ahead of code; HISTORICAL docs are context only. Discrepancies are reported, not papered over."}, {"id": "agents_progressive_disclosure", "label": "Progressive Disclosure Workflow", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Before non-trivial work: understand scope, consult docs/README.md, inspect current code, identify tests, then plan and execute."}, {"id": "agents_verification_matrix", "label": "Verification Matrix by Change Type", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Minimum checks per change type; tables/service days/reservations run test:table-crud, rooms-map, reservations, reservation-sheet, table-layouts (renamed from table-merge-layouts) and service-days. npm test chains every listed suite; Playwright e2e specs are outside it and run in CI only on pull requests."}], "edges": [{"source": "agents", "target": "docs_readme", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "agents_services_routes_boundary", "target": "readme_service_days", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "agents_offline_first_invariant", "target": "frontend_src_lib_features", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "agents_offline_first_invariant", "target": "main_features", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "agents_progressive_disclosure", "target": "docs_readme", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "agents_no_joined_tables", "target":